Yes, this is the version I was using before compiling under Cygwin with
Qt, but it is significantly different than the Qt version.  The windows
native version doesn't do any of the nice stat change highlighting or
confusion/stun icons which I find really hepful (the Qt version also
changes the color of the box around your character accoring to HP
level).  I also prefer having the stats at the top right instead of
below the map.  So, IMHO, the Qt version is much better than the native
Win port but perhaps I'm in the minority there.

I might see if I can figure out how to do a native MinGW compile that
doesn't require the Cygwin runtime libraries.  Cygwin GCC can compile
native Windows binaries using the MinGW extensions, this works quite
well.  The trick might be getting a native (i.e. non Cygwin) Windows Qt
library.



